# Git LFS for the brand binaries.
#
# Same anchoring reason as tv-menu/.gitattributes: the root file's patterns all
# contain a slash, so they are anchored to the repo root and do not reach into
# brand/. Without a rule here the primary lockup — a 3 MB PNG — would land in
# git as a raw blob.
#
# The root .gitattributes has an UNCOMMITTED change from another session that
# adds equivalent brand/** rules. When that lands, this file becomes redundant
# and should be deleted rather than left to disagree with it. It exists now so
# the logo can be committed without touching that unfinished work.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: brand.json and README.md. They are the part a human
# reviews, and a brand change must show up as a readable diff ("hot pink moved
# from #F20A88 to ...") rather than as an opaque LFS pointer swap.
logos/*.png      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
logos/*.PNG      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
logos/*.svg      -filter -diff -merge text
guidelines/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
